## Working rules

- Never redesign locked sections unless the user specifically asks.
- Touch only the assigned section in a sprint.
- Prefer Kindred paper tokens (`newspaperTheme`) over reference brand palettes.

## Homepage Editorial Design Standard (permanent)

Kindred is a **modern morning newspaper, not a social media feed.** The homepage
must feel clean, elegant, fast, and easy to scan.

**Standard homepage sections — text-first, no listing photos:** Local Events ·
Activities · Food & Drinks · Local News · National News · Bandit's Picks.

**Display only:** appropriate emoji(s) · headline · one- or two-sentence
editorial summary · city · editorial badges (Free, 21+, Dog Friendly, etc.).

**Do not** display photographs or thumbnail images on these homepage listings.
The emoji is the visual identifier — accurate and context-specific; multiple
emojis allowed when clarity improves; never generic when a better match exists.

**Article pages** — where Kindred becomes visual: authorized feature image,
additional authorized images, Maps, website, hours, address, parking, contact,
tickets, verified details.

**Image policy:** official, licensed, public domain, Creative Commons (with
attribution), government, museum/library, business, or organizer supplied only.
**Never** AI-generated images · never fabricated images · never AI artwork
pretending to represent a real place, business, event, or person. No authorized
image → clean layout without an image.

**Homepage exceptions (feature stories, not listings):** Today's Masterpiece ·
Story of Your City · Today in History · History Around Town — may keep large
feature artwork on the homepage.

**Principle:** The homepage is today's front page. The article is where
photography belongs. Maintain across all future development.
